## Getting started

The full lifecycle — install the launcher once, scaffold, provision, run:

```bash
# 1. Install the dude launcher globally (private package — needs the token above).
#    This is the ONLY global install. It auto-runs each project's pinned CLI.
npm install -g @cubocicloide/dude-launcher

# 2. Scaffold the project (this is how {{projectName}} was created).
dude init {{projectName}} --stack react-fastapi
cd {{projectName}}

# 3. Provision the project toolchain — installs the pinned `dude` CLI + stack
#    (and root dev deps) from the lockfile.
pnpm install

# 4. First run — build the images and start every service.
dude up --build

# 5. From the second run onward, just:
dude up
```

> **Already have the project?** If you're reading this inside `{{projectName}}`
> (or you just `git clone`d it), it's already scaffolded — skip step 2 and start
> at `pnpm install`.

> **How `dude` resolves its version.** `dude` on your `PATH` is the *launcher*.
> On the first `dude <cmd>` inside a project it provisions the versions pinned in
> `package.json` (running `pnpm install` for you if `node_modules` is missing),
> then re-execs the project-local CLI. So step 3 is optional — `dude up --build`
> would trigger it — but running it explicitly makes the first build faster and
> surfaces any auth problem up front.

