### Documentation site

This project ships a full docs site (MkDocs Material). Serve it locally:

```bash
dude docs                 # → http://localhost:8001
dude docs --port 9000     # custom port
```

It live-reloads as you edit files under `docs/docs/`. The **Command reference**
page is auto-generated from your actual commands every time you run `dude docs`.

### Hot reload

- **Frontend** — Vite HMR is on by default. Edit any file under `frontend/src/`
  and the browser updates instantly without a full page reload.
- **Backend** — Uvicorn runs with `--reload`. Edit any Python file under
  `backend/app/` and the API restarts automatically within a second.

### Common commands

| Command | Description |
|---------|-------------|
| `dude up --build` | Rebuild images and start all services |
| `dude up` | Start all services (detached) |
| `dude down` | Stop and remove containers |
| `dude logs [service]` | Follow logs (omit service to follow all) |
| `dude shell <service>` | Open a shell inside a running container |
| `dude api sync` | Fetch OpenAPI spec → regenerate typed client |
| `dude api review` | Validate generated client against the spec |
| `dude lint` | Run all stack lint checks |
| `dude docs` | Serve this documentation (http://localhost:8001) |
| `dude help` | Live list of every available command |
| `dude upgrade` | Update pinned CLI and stack versions for this project |

Run `dude help` for the full, live catalog (it reflects this project's `dude
init` choices), or see the **Working with dude** page in the docs site.

### Upgrading pinned versions

Use `dude upgrade` to update the versions pinned in `package.json` and
`dude.json`.

```bash
dude upgrade
dude upgrade --cli --cli-version 0.6.1
dude upgrade --stack --stack-version 5.0.5
```

This updates version pins only; it does not migrate existing files. Run `pnpm
install` afterwards. To roll back, pin the previous version again and reinstall:

```bash
dude upgrade --cli --cli-version 0.6.0
dude upgrade --stack --stack-version 5.0.4
pnpm install
```

